  "behavior_trace": [
    "Importing ty only exposes find_ty_bin. python -m ty locates the installed binary via Python sysconfig and launches it with argv using execvp on Unix or subprocess.run on Windows.",
    "Rust main calls ty::run; the CLI dispatches Check, Server, Version, GenerateShellCompletion and Explain. Check discovers project files, parses Python and checks types; fix/watch modes are explicit options.",
    "Cargo ty/build.rs reads dist-workspace.toml and optional Git metadata; ty_vendored/build.rs zips local typeshed sources; no release-to-release build script changes.",
    "mdtest create_diagnostic_snapshot prints source with line-number gutters and diagnostics. Its comment explicitly says the result is invalid Python. Abstract methods in the flagged snapshots have ellipsis bodies. Carets underline a diagnostic; they are not XOR operations.",
    "Vendored posix.pyi, nt.pyi and sqlite3/__init__.pyi contain standard-library type declarations/imports consumed by the checker; these declarations do not execute their named APIs.",
    "Archive facts and both flagged files were examined with cleave facts, including literals, symbols and flow. The snapshots have no function-definition symbols and no decoded executable payload."
  ],
